\label{sec:observer-comparison}
\subsubsection{Ten-seed OU-family comparison}
The stationary JONSWAP primary endpoint is
$\OUValidationOUIIINormalizedMean\pm\OUValidationOUIIINormalizedStd\%$ of
$H_s$ for OU--III versus
$\OUValidationOUIINormalizedMean\pm\OUValidationOUIINormalizedStd\%$ for
OU--II. The paired difference is
$\OUValidationNormalizedDifference$ percentage points, with bootstrap 95\%
interval $[\OUValidationNormalizedDifferenceLow,\OUValidationNormalizedDifferenceHigh]$
and exact sign-flip $p=\OUValidationNormalizedRandomizationP$.
Figure~\ref{fig:ou_mc_vertical} shows lower OU--III vertical error in all
four stationary seas. Full 3-D RMS is also lower, with paired intervals
excluding zero (Fig.~\ref{fig:ou_mc_displacement}); individual horizontal
channels need not improve. Pitch is shown in Fig.~\ref{fig:ou_mc_pitch}.

PM--Stokes is analyzed separately rather than pooled with JONSWAP.
Its ensemble gives a normalized vertical difference of
$\OUValidationPMStokesDifference$ percentage points with interval
$[\OUValidationPMStokesDifferenceLow,\OUValidationPMStokesDifferenceHigh]$.
This supports transfer between the two prescribed spectral families, not
uncertainty over other hulls or headings.

