\subsubsection{Paired TFG comparison}
The TFG study uses the same ten seed triplets, eight stationary records, and
controlled crossfade, with both estimators' settings frozen. Its generated
``JONSWAP'' aggregate includes the four stationary seas \emph{and the
crossfade}. For seed $i$, the actual reported contrast is
\begin{equation}
 d_i=\frac{1}{5}\left(\sum_{h=1}^{4}\Delta E_{Z,i,h}
                  +\Delta E_{Z,i,\mathrm{crossfade}}\right),
 \qquad \Delta E_Z=E_Z^{\mathrm{TFG}}-E_Z^{\mathrm{OU\text{-}III}}.
 \label{eq:tfg-reported-aggregate}
\end{equation}
Here $E_Z=100\,\mathrm{RMS}(\hat z-z)/H_s$; the crossfade uses the final
$H_s=\SI{4}{m}$. This five-condition pooling explains the OU--III baseline
$4.423\%$, versus $4.35\%$ in the four-stationary-sea primary endpoint;
the underlying OU--III replay results are identical. The bootstrap resamples
ten seed-level differences, not the individual conditions.

\input{w3d-tfg-comparison-generated.tex-part}
Tables~\ref{tab:tfg-paired} and \ref{tab:tfg-ensembles} show a small
OU--III heave advantage in the mixed aggregate and the separate PM--Stokes
ensemble, lower gyroscope-bias error for TFG, and no resolved crossfade
heave advantage. Other channels are exploratory without multiplicity
adjustment. This comparison tests complete estimators, not Lie-group
coordinates in isolation; TFG wave-direction outputs are not scored.

The bidirectional transient diagnostic is reported in Sec.~\ref{sec:roundtrip-transition-ablation}.

